  2W/eta=O_eta(D)

physical crossing edges. Every surviving component lies in one sixfold-phase bin, hence in three projective direction cones of width <=eta/6.

No minimum-degree pruning is needed for coherence.

Small train components v<rho D carry at most
  (C_T rho/4)D^2
crossings total.
Sparse macroscopic components e<kappa vD carry at most
  kappa C_TD^2.

Every remaining dense macroscopic grain has a phase pair of crossing density >=kappa/(3C_T) and both shores >=kappa D/3, so PDG gives a complete Omega(D) grid.

Next: use MG3-MG4 + PC3/MCP on this boundary-order-interface decomposition.
```
